course: dictionary
lesson: 15121
title: Samurai: warriors of old Japan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word is easier to understand when you read the words around it. «The samurai polished his sword before the battle.» Polishing a sword and going into battle tells you that a samurai is a fighter.
explain: A samurai was a warrior in old Japan who served a lord. «The samurai guarded the lord's castle gate.» The word guarded tells you the samurai's job was to protect someone important.
explain: Samurai also means the whole warrior class of people in Japanese history. They lived there from about the 12th century until the 1870s, when their class was ended. Their code of honour, called bushido, valued loyalty and courage.
fact: A samurai was a warrior in old Japan who served a lord.
fact: Samurai fought with swords and bows.
fact: The samurai were a class of people in Japanese history, lasting from about the 12th century until the 1870s.
fact: Samurai followed a code of honour called bushido, which valued loyalty and courage.
fact: The word samurai stays the same in the plural: one samurai, many samurai.
exercise: «The samurai polished his sword before the battle.» What is a samurai most likely to be? | *A warrior who served a lord | A king who lived in a palace | A teacher in a school | A farmer who grew rice
exercise: A samurai followed a code of honour called bushido. What did this code value most? | Speed and silence | *Loyalty and courage | Singing and dancing | Wealth and big houses
exercise: «The samurai carried a long sword and a bow.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the samurai fought with. | long | *sword | carried | the
test: «The samurai served his lord faithfully for many years.» What does served mean here? | *Worked for and protected | Ate dinner with | Lost track of | Painted a picture of
test: In which country did the samurai live? | *Japan | Korea | China | Mongolia
exam: Ella says a samurai is just a sword fighter from a film. Why is she only partly right? | Samurai were a kind of food from Japan | Samurai only appear in games, never in history | *Samurai were real warriors in Japan, and they also belonged to a class of people in history | Samurai were a real class of warriors in Japanese history, not only film characters
